'''Bistan''' was a [[Gender|male]] [[Iakaru]] [[Rebel trooper|soldier]] who served as a [[corporal]] in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]]. He participated in the [[Battle of Scarif]], as door-gunner for an Alliance [[UT-60D U-wing starfighter/support craft|U-wing]].

==Biography==
[[File:Bistan-AG.png|thumb|left|200px|Bistan joined the Rebel Alliance about six months prior to the Battle of Scarif]]
Bistan joined the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] approximately six [[Standard month|months]] prior to the [[Battle of Scarif]]. [[Gender|He]] aided a team of [[Rebel Alliance Special Forces]] who had [[Infiltration of Iakar|infiltrated]] his [[homeworld]] of [[Iakar]] to steal medical supplies, by fending off their [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] pursuers with accurately-thrown [[spear]]s and rocks. Bistan proved to be such a skilled marksman under [[fire]] that he was invited by the SpecForce [[Rebel Commando|commandos]] to join the rebellion.<ref name="Visual Guide" />

Bistan was present on [[Yavin 4]] when [[Jyn Erso]] shared information about her [[Galen Walton Erso|father's]] sabotage to the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]], with the Rebel Alliance. Once Jyn's speech was over, Bistan was among the rebels who cheered. The Alliance feared extreme [[Death|casualties]], however, and did not support sending rebel forces on a mission to Scarif to help steal the [[Death Star plans]]. Despite his excitement, Bistan did not defy orders.<ref name="Rogue One" />

Nevertheless, Bistan and many others were later sent to Scarif as reinforcements, after [[Admiral]] [[Raddus]] had departed to join the unsanctioned operation begun by [[Rogue One]]. Bistan served as the [[gunner]] of a [[Blue Squadron (Rebel Alliance)|Blue Squadron]] [[UT-60D U-wing starfighter/support craft|U-wing]] piloted by [[Laren Joma]], and opened fire on an [[All Terrain Armored Cargo Transport]] immediately upon arrival,<ref name="Rogue One" /> using the ship's door-mounted [["Roba" M-45 repeating ion blaster]].<ref name="Visual Guide" /> His salvos eventually weakened and pierced one of the walker's legs, causing the entire walker to collapse. Later during the battle, however, one of the U-Wing's [[engine]]s was struck by a [[laser]], causing the [[Starship|ship]] to crash into the ground and explode, killing Bistan and the rest of the crew.<ref name="Rogue One" />

==Personality and traits==
[[File:Bistan-CT.png|thumb|right|200px|Bistan had excepional spatial awareness and quick reflexes.]]
Described as a fierce warrior, Bistan was a short, [[Color|light]]-skinned Iakaru, covered in black [[hair]], with orange [[eye]]s.<ref name="SW Show 36" /> Like other Iakaru, Bistan possessed exceptional spatial awareness and quick reflexes, as well as keen eyesight and accurate depth perception.<ref name="Visual Guide" /> He served as a door [[gunner]] on a UT-60D U-wing starfighter/support craft.<ref name="Star Wars Show Episode 11">{{StarWarsShow|JGCR89WQ87g|Exclusive Chat with Alden Ehrenreich and Details on Rogue One's Space Monkey|sw_url=video/the-star-wars-show-episode-11}}</ref> While manning his weapon, Bistan used minimal safety restraints, and relied more so upon his agility and innate sense of balance to stay aboard.<ref name="Visual Guide" /> Even though he wanted to ensure the freedom of fellow Iakaru, he really fought for the action and thrill of combat.<ref name="Bistan DB" /> Bistan was popular among fellow rebels, due to his unending gregarious energy, though his personnel file did list multiple incidents of insubordination.<ref name="Visual Guide" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|It's Nick's eyes we see, not lenses. The reason I think Chewbacca works so well is that you actually see Chewie's eyes. It's a real person's eyes and that makes all the difference.|Neal Scanlan|<ref name="Mission Debrief">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story - The Official Mission Debrief]]''</ref>}}
Bistan is a character portrayed by [[Nick Kellington]] in the [[2016]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|anthology]] film, ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''.<ref name="Rogue One" /> Concept art of the character was done by [[Ivan Manzella]] and [[Adam Brockbank]].<ref name="ArtofRO">''[[The Art of Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> His name and race were revealed by [[Pablo Hidalgo]] on ''[[The Star Wars Show]]'' on [[July 20]], [[2016]].<ref name="Star Wars Show Episode 11" /> The character was known as "space monkey" to the crew.<ref name="Creature feature">{{SWYouTube|qV_dg8Citm4|The Creatures, Droids and Aliens of Star Wars: The Force Awakens &#124; Star Wars Celebration Europe 2016}}</ref> Like the character [[Chewbacca]], actor Nick Kellington's eyes were visible through the suit instead of lenses. According to [[Neal Scanlan]], the creature effects supervisor for ''Rogue One'', the sight of a real person's eyes contributed to the appeal of Bistan's character, along with the "space monkey" design that director [[Gareth Edwards]] immediately liked for its amusing and playful quality.<ref name="Mission Debrief" />

They first appeared prior to the release of the film, in the [[Star Wars video games|mobile video game]] ''[[Star Wars: Galaxy of Heroes]]'' on November 1, 2016.<ref name="GoH forums">{{EA|subdomain=forums.galaxy-of-heroes.starwars|url=discussion/74049/game-update-10-27-2016|text=Game Update - 10/27/2016|archivedate=20170225204713|nolive=1}}</ref>

